  "notes": [
    "-AR verb with orthographic spelling change: g→gu before *e* (pegué, pegue, peguemos, peguen) to preserve the hard [g] sound",
    "Same pattern as *llegar*, *pagar*, *jugar*",
    "Past participle: *pegado*",
    "*pegar algo* = to stick/glue something (*Pega el sello en el sobre* — Stick the stamp on the envelope)",
    "*pegar a alguien* = to hit someone (*No pegues a tu hermano* — Don't hit your brother)",
    "*pegar un grito/salto/susto* = to let out a scream / to jump / to give a fright",
    "*pegarse* (reflexive) = to stick to each other; to hit oneself; to be catchy (*Esta canción se pega mucho* — This song is very catchy)",
    "*no pegar ojo* = to not sleep a wink",
    "Related: *el pegamento* = glue; *pegajoso/a* = sticky, catchy"
  ],
  "sourceFile": "Verbs/p/Pegar.md"
